   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Rush Type\n\nWhite words blast into vertical RGB shutter trails, one forceful word at a time: the word falls out of perspective, stretches into a tall red/green/blue-fringed smear, snaps to a sharp readable rest, then blasts away as the next word arrives. The fringing comes from motion alone, not from tinting the text; a tube mask and glow ride along with the blast. WebGL, over an opaque background colour.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3.4667 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A short phrase should cycle one forceful word at a time.\n- Chromatic separation should emerge from motion rather than tinting the text.\n- A kinetic-type beat needs a sharp readable rest between extreme blasts.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text must remain readable throughout the motion: use word-push or zoom-words.\n- You want a horizontal digital glitch: use rgb-glitch-text.\n- The block must remain transparent: it always paints an opaque background.\n\nVariables:\n- phrase (string): Phrase, default \"gone before you look\"\n- font_size (number, 32-140): Resting size, default 68\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"400\"\n- color (color): Text colour, default \"#ffffff\"\n- background_color (color): Background, default \"#000000\"\n- vertical_stretch (number, 3-12): Vertical stretch, default 7\n- chromatic_spread (number, 0-2): Chromatic spread, default 1\n- rest_duration (number, 6-30): Rest duration, default 12\n- peak_hold_duration (number, 0-15): Peak hold, default 3\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
